---
/*
  ============================================================
  SUBSTANCE — publication-quiet variant
  Route: /variants/substance/
  ============================================================

  Posture: a writer's portal, not a brochure. This is the front
  page of a small publication. The work is the proof; the offer
  is whispered.

  Reference operators: Jane Portman / UI Breakfast (podcast as
  hub), Corey Haines / corey.co (multi-venture portal,
  content-first), Val Geisler (weekly teardowns as authority
  signal).

  ----- Layout choice -----
  BaseLayout is SKIPPED on purpose.

  Reasons:
   1. BaseLayout pulls in <Nav>, which is hard-coded to the
      "About / Lead Magnet / Behavioral Emails / Book a Call"
      structure and a Calendly CTA. The Substance page wants a
      publication nav: "Teardowns · Writing · Method · Work ·
      About" — five items, no CTA pill, no badge.
   2. BaseLayout imports global.css which loads Inter and sets
      `font-size: 19px` plus a sans-serif body. A publication
      front needs a serif body and quieter base size. Loading
      global.css would force an override war.
   3. We need our own font links in <head> (Source Serif 4 +
      Inter), and our own theme tokens, scoped to the page.
   4. The brief says "you may use BaseLayout or skip it";
      everything we'd keep from it (favicon, meta tags, the
      reveal observer) is small enough to inline cleanly.

  Constraint check: scoped styles only — handled by writing all
  page CSS inside <style> in this file. No edits to /src/styles
  or any sibling component.
  ============================================================
*/

const pageTitle = 'First Action Fix — Teardowns and writing on trial-to-paid for sales-tech SaaS.';
const pageDescription = 'Trial-to-paid teardowns for sales-tech SaaS founders. One per Tuesday. Public. Named. Free.';
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="description" content={pageDescription} />
    <title>{pageTitle}</title>

    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/x-icon" href="/favicon.ico" sizes="32x32" />

    {/*
      ----- Font pairing -----
      BODY: Source Serif 4 — a contemporary literary serif with
      true italics and a calm rhythm at long-form widths. It
      reads as "magazine essay" without the dryness of a textbook
      serif. Picked over Lora (too rounded for a teardown's clinical
      voice), Newsreader (slightly too display-flavoured for body),
      and Spectral (great but heavier vertical color).

      META / NAV: Inter — already familiar to the codebase, used
      tightly here at small sizes for dates, word counts, nav
      labels. Inter at 0.78–0.92rem reads as "publication chrome"
      not "marketing UI" once we drop the bold weights.

      Together: serif body anchors the page as content-forward;
      Inter handles the chrome. Two voices, one reading mode.
    */}
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@400;500;600&family=Source+Serif+4:ital,opsz,wght@0,8..60,400;0,8..60,500;0,8..60,600;0,8..60,700;1,8..60,400&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
  </head>

  <body>
    {/*
      ============================================================
      HEADER — publication style
      Full nav visible. No CTA pill. Wordmark + five quiet links.
      A thin rule under the nav, the way a masthead gets a hairline.
      ============================================================
    */}
    <header class="masthead">
      <div class="masthead__inner">
        <a href="/variants/substance/" class="masthead__wordmark">First Action Fix</a>
        <nav class="masthead__nav" aria-label="Publication">
          <a href="#teardowns">Teardowns</a>
          <a href="#writing">Writing</a>
          <a href="#method">Method</a>
          <a href="#work">Work</a>
          <a href="#about">About</a>
        </nav>
      </div>
    </header>

    <main>
      {/*
        ============================================================
        HERO — title and tagline only.
        A publication doesn't shout. The H1 is medium weight, set in
        the serif at a size below the article-title cap. The tagline
        is a single line, slightly muted. No buttons here.
        ============================================================
      */}
      <section class="hero">
        <div class="container container--prose">
          <h1 class="hero__title">Trial-to-paid teardowns for sales-tech SaaS founders.</h1>
          <p class="hero__tagline">One per Tuesday. Public. Named. Free.</p>
          <p class="hero__cadence">
            <span class="dot" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            Teardowns published every Tuesday, starting May&nbsp;5,&nbsp;2026.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="rule" />

      {/*
        ============================================================
        LATEST TEARDOWN — featured card #1
        Featured cards are wider, breathe more, and use the serif
        for the article title at a real "headline" size. The dek
        sits below in a slightly smaller serif italic-eligible
        weight; the body excerpt is a normal paragraph.
        ============================================================
      */}
      <section id="teardowns" class="featured reveal">
        <div class="container container--prose">
          <p class="kicker">Latest teardown</p>
          <p class="meta">Tuesday, May 5, 2026 <span class="meta-sep">·</span> 3,200 words</p>
          <h2 class="article-title">
            <a href="#">
              <span class="article-title__subject">[Smartlead]</span>
              <span class="article-title__sep">·</span>
              Where the trial flow loses 60% of qualified signups before they send their first sequence.
            </a>
          </h2>
          <p class="article-dek">
            The activation event for any cold email tool is "first sequence sent." Smartlead's trial requires
            deliverability configuration, list import, and template setup before that event can fire — three
            setup tasks that lose users at predictable points.
          </p>
          {/* eventual destination: /teardowns/smartlead/ */}
          <a href="#" class="read-more">Read the teardown <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="rule rule--soft" />

      {/*
        ============================================================
        LATEST ESSAY — featured card #2
        Same pattern as the teardown card so the page reads as a
        repeated form. Keeps the rhythm. Distinguishing this from
        the teardown card visually would weaken the "publication
        index" feel — both are publication items, treat them the
        same.
        ============================================================
      */}
      <section id="writing" class="featured reveal">
        <div class="container container--prose">
          <p class="kicker">Latest essay</p>
          <p class="meta">April 28, 2026 <span class="meta-sep">·</span> 1,800 words</p>
          <h2 class="article-title">
            <a href="#">
              Why "increase trial-to-paid conversion" is the wrong goal for any SaaS measuring activation correctly.
            </a>
          </h2>
          <p class="article-dek">
            Trial-to-paid is a lagging indicator with too few events to move reliably on small traffic.
            Activation-by-day-7 has 3–5x the event volume and responds to interventions faster.
          </p>
          {/* eventual destination: /writing/wrong-number-to-chase/ */}
          <a href="#" class="read-more">Read the essay <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="rule rule--soft" />

      {/*
        ============================================================
        THE METHOD — third card variant.
        Distinguished from the publication items because it is a
        standalone resource, not an issue. Visual treatment:
         · framed by a quiet inset panel (warm tinted bg, subtle
           border) instead of being flush like an essay.
         · kicker label reads "Free resource" not a date.
         · the link is a button-like link (still text, just bolder
           and wrapped) rather than the inline arrow used by
           publication items.
        Same content posture though — calm, no exclamation.
        ============================================================
      */}
      <section id="method" class="method reveal">
        <div class="container container--prose">
          <div class="method__panel">
            <p class="kicker kicker--muted">Free resource</p>
            <h2 class="method__title">The Method</h2>
            <p class="method__lede">
              A free 6-email course on installing trial-to-paid systems in sales-tech SaaS.
            </p>
            <p class="method__body">
              Covers the activation gap, the displacement principle, and the orchestration layer
              that pairs structured education with behavioral triggers.
            </p>
            <p class="method__body method__body--quiet">
              For founders who've already read enough teardowns to know the next move is system-shaped.
            </p>
            {/* eventual destination: /eec/ or /method/ */}
            <a href="#" class="method__cta">Start the course <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <hr class="rule" />

      {/*
        ============================================================
        ARCHIVE — two stacked lists with date dot-leaders.
        No card chrome, no hover lift. Tight line-height. This is
        the "what else have you written" list a returning reader
        scans. Density is the point. Stays still on scroll — no
        reveal class on archive items.
        ============================================================
      */}
      <section class="archive">
        <div class="container container--prose">
          <div class="archive__group">
            <h3 class="archive__heading">Recent teardowns</h3>
            <ul class="archive__list">
              <li><span class="archive__name">Apollo</span><span class="archive__leader" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="archive__date">April 28</span></li>
              <li><span class="archive__name">Lemlist</span><span class="archive__leader" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="archive__date">April 21</span></li>
              <li><span class="archive__name">Instantly</span><span class="archive__leader" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="archive__date">April 14</span></li>
              <li><span class="archive__name">Heyreach</span><span class="archive__leader" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="archive__date">April 7</span></li>
            </ul>
            {/* eventual destination: /teardowns/ */}
            <a href="#" class="archive__more">All teardowns <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
          </div>

          <div class="archive__group">
            <h3 class="archive__heading">Recent writing</h3>
            <ul class="archive__list">
              <li><span class="archive__name">The wrong number to chase</span><span class="archive__leader" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="archive__date">April 14</span></li>
              <li><span class="archive__name">Activation requires displacement, not addition</span><span class="archive__leader" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="archive__date">March 31</span></li>
              <li><span class="archive__name">Why behavioral triggers and structured education compound only when paired</span><span class="archive__leader" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="archive__date">March 17</span></li>
            </ul>
            {/* eventual destination: /writing/ */}
            <a href="#" class="archive__more">All writing <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      {/*
        ============================================================
        QUIET FOOTER
        Service link is a single soft sentence, then the colophon.
        No big CTA. The reader who wants to hire scrolls down to
        find the link; the reader who came to read isn't shouted at.
        ============================================================
      */}
      <footer id="work" class="colophon">
        <div class="container container--prose">
          <p class="colophon__work">
            Looking to work together? See <a href="#" class="colophon__service-link">services <span class="arrow">&rarr;</span></a>
          </p>
          <p class="colophon__line" id="about">
            First Action Fix <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            By Andrew Z. <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            Poznań <span class="meta-sep">·</span>
            <a href="mailto:adennagleng@gmail.com" class="colophon__contact">Contact</a>
          </p>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </main>

    {/*
      ============================================================
      Scroll-reveal observer.
      Inlined here because we skipped BaseLayout. Only the two
      featured cards (.reveal) animate in. Archive list, method
      panel, footer — all static. The voice is calm; over-animating
      this page would betray the posture.
      ============================================================
    */}
    <script>
      const reveals = document.querySelectorAll('.reveal');
      if ('IntersectionObserver' in window) {
        const obs = new IntersectionObserver(
          (entries) => {
            entries.forEach((entry) => {
              if (entry.isIntersecting) {
                entry.target.classList.add('is-revealed');
                obs.unobserve(entry.target);
              }
            });
          },
          { threshold: 0.12 }
        );
        reveals.forEach((el) => obs.observe(el));
      } else {
        reveals.forEach((el) => el.classList.add('is-revealed'));
      }
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
  /*
    ============================================================
    PALETTE — paper-quiet
    ----- Why this set reads as editorial -----
    --paper:  #F7F4EC  warm off-white, slight cream cast. Not
                       white. White feels like a SaaS dashboard;
                       cream feels like uncoated stock.
    --ink:    #1C1A17  warm dark, not pure black. Pairs with the
                       cream the way printed text sits on a page.
    --ink-2:  #4A453E  body and dek — softened ink for paragraphs.
    --ink-3:  #8A8278  meta info (dates, word counts, leaders).
                       Low contrast on purpose; metadata should
                       defer to titles.
    --rule:   #DAD3C4  hairline rules — visible but not a divider
                       wall.
    --accent: #8A4B2C  burnt sienna. Restrained. Used only on
                       links and the cadence dot. Never on a
                       background, never on a button.
    --panel:  #EFEADF   Method panel tint — same family as paper,
                       one step warmer/darker, so the panel reads
                       as a quoted block, not a card.

    The page never uses pure white or pure black. That's the
    discipline that makes it read as a publication rather than
    a marketing site.
    ============================================================
  */
  :global(html) {
    font-size: 18px;
    -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased;
    -moz-osx-font-smoothing: grayscale;
  }

  :global(body) {
    margin: 0;
    background: #F7F4EC;
    color: #1C1A17;
    font-family: 'Source Serif 4', 'Source Serif Pro', Georgia, 'Iowan Old Style', serif;
    font-feature-settings: "kern", "liga", "onum";
    line-height: 1.6;
    text-rendering: optimizeLegibility;
  }

  :global(*, *::before, *::after) {
    box-sizing: border-box;
  }

  :global(a) {
    color: inherit;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  :global(ul) {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }

  :global(p) {
    margin: 0;
  }

  :global(img) {
    max-width: 100%;
    display: block;
  }

  /* Local CSS variables, scoped to the page tree we render. */
  main, header, footer {
    --paper: #F7F4EC;
    --ink: #1C1A17;
    --ink-2: #4A453E;
    --ink-3: #8A8278;
    --rule: #DAD3C4;
    --rule-soft: #E6DFCD;
    --accent: #8A4B2C;
    --accent-hover: #6E3B22;
    --panel: #EFEADF;
    --sans: 'Inter', system-ui, -apple-system, 'Segoe UI', sans-serif;
    --serif: 'Source Serif 4', 'Source Serif Pro', Georgia, 'Iowan Old Style', serif;
  }

  /* ----- Layout containers ----- */
  .container {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 1080px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .container--prose {
    max-width: 720px;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     MASTHEAD
     A publication header. Wordmark left, nav right. Hairline
     under it. Full width but never wider than the container.
     ============================================================ */
  .masthead {
    background: var(--paper);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .masthead__inner {
    max-width: 1080px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1.4rem 1.5rem;
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 2rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .masthead__wordmark {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1.15rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.005em;
    color: var(--ink);
  }
  .masthead__nav {
    display: flex;
    gap: 1.6rem;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
  }
  .masthead__nav a {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.005em;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    transition: color 160ms ease;
  }
  .masthead__nav a:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }

  /* ============================================================
     HERO
     H1 sits at clamp(1.7rem, 3.2vw, 2.4rem) — small for a hero.
     A publication doesn't shout. Article titles get more weight
     than this. Tagline is one line, slightly muted, sans.
     ============================================================ */
  .hero {
    padding: 5.5rem 0 3rem;
  }
  .hero__title {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 500;
    font-size: clamp(1.7rem, 3.2vw, 2.4rem);
    line-height: 1.18;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
    color: var(--ink);
    max-width: 22ch;
    margin: 0 0 1.1rem;
  }
  .hero__tagline {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }
  .hero__cadence {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.55rem;
  }
  .hero__cadence .dot {
    width: 6px;
    height: 6px;
    border-radius: 50%;
    background: var(--accent);
    display: inline-block;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     RULES
     Two weights — one full hairline, one softer between sibling
     publication items.
     ============================================================ */
  .rule {
    border: 0;
    height: 1px;
    background: var(--rule);
    max-width: 1080px;
    margin: 1rem auto;
  }
  .rule--soft {
    background: var(--rule-soft);
  }

  /* ============================================================
     FEATURED CARDS — teardown + essay
     No box, no border, no background. The "card" is white space
     plus typography. Wider vertical padding than the archive.
     The article title is the visual anchor.
     ============================================================ */
  .featured {
    padding: 3rem 0;
  }

  .kicker {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin: 0 0 0.65rem;
  }
  .kicker--muted {
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .meta {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
    font-feature-settings: "tnum";
  }
  .meta-sep {
    margin: 0 0.4rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
  }

  .article-title {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 2.6vw, 1.95rem);
    line-height: 1.22;
    letter-spacing: -0.012em;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .article-title a {
    background-image: linear-gradient(var(--accent), var(--accent));
    background-size: 0 1px;
    background-repeat: no-repeat;
    background-position: 0 95%;
    transition: background-size 240ms ease, color 160ms ease;
  }
  .article-title a:hover {
    background-size: 100% 1px;
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .article-title__subject {
    color: var(--accent);
    font-style: italic;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .article-title__sep {
    color: var(--ink-3);
    margin: 0 0.25rem;
    font-weight: 400;
  }

  .article-dek {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
    max-width: 62ch;
  }

  .read-more {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.88rem;
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--accent);
    border-bottom: 1px solid transparent;
    transition: border-color 160ms ease, color 160ms ease;
    padding-bottom: 1px;
  }
  .read-more:hover {
    color: var(--accent-hover);
    border-bottom-color: var(--accent-hover);
  }
  .arrow {
    display: inline-block;
    transition: transform 200ms ease;
  }
  .read-more:hover .arrow {
    transform: translateX(2px);
  }

  /* ============================================================
     METHOD PANEL
     Inset panel, warmer tint than the page. Reads as a quoted
     block — distinct from publication items. The CTA here is a
     bolder text link with a top hairline above it, like a pull-
     quote attribution.
     ============================================================ */
  .method {
    padding: 3rem 0;
  }
  .method__panel {
    background: var(--panel);
    border: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-radius: 2px;  /* very square — feels like print, not UI */
    padding: 2.4rem 2rem 2.2rem;
  }
  .method__title {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 2.6vw, 2rem);
    letter-spacing: -0.015em;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
  }
  .method__lede {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0 0 0.85rem;
    max-width: 56ch;
  }
  .method__body {
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1rem;
    color: var(--ink-2);
    margin: 0 0 0.7rem;
    max-width: 60ch;
  }
  .method__body--quiet {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    margin-bottom: 1.4rem;
  }
  .method__cta {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.92rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--ink);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    padding-top: 0.9rem;
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
    transition: color 160ms ease;
  }
  .method__cta:hover {
    color: var(--accent);
  }
  .method__cta:hover .arrow {
    transform: translateX(2px);
  }
  .method__cta .arrow {
    transition: transform 200ms ease;
  }

  /* ============================================================
     ARCHIVE
     Two stacked groups, each a tight list with dot-leaders.
     No card. No hover lift. Density on purpose.
     The dot-leader is a flex item with a dotted bottom border.
     ============================================================ */
  .archive {
    padding: 3.5rem 0 4rem;
  }
  .archive__group {
    margin-bottom: 2.6rem;
  }
  .archive__group:last-child {
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .archive__heading {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.7rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.14em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }
  .archive__list {
    margin: 0 0 0.9rem;
  }
  .archive__list li {
    display: flex;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: 0.6rem;
    padding: 0.45rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule-soft);
    font-family: var(--serif);
    font-size: 1rem;
    line-height: 1.4;
  }
  .archive__list li:last-child {
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  .archive__name {
    color: var(--ink);
    flex-shrink: 1;
    min-width: 0;
  }
  .archive__leader {
    flex: 1 1 auto;
    border-bottom: 1px dotted var(--ink-3);
    transform: translateY(-3px);
    margin: 0 0.2rem;
    min-width: 1.5rem;
  }
  .archive__date {
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--ink-3);
    flex-shrink: 0;
    font-feature-settings: "tnum";
  }
  .archive__more {
    display: inline-block;
    font-family: var(--sans);
    font-size: 0.82rem;
    color: var(--accent);
    margin-top: 0.4rem;
    transition: color 160ms ease;
  }
  .archive__more:hover {
    color: var(--accent-hover);
  }
